Regardless of what interface you use, you can always put

	OPTIONS=Name:YourNameHere

in your .nethackrc or defaults.nh or whatever file, and you'll thereby skip 
the name prompt.

You can even do something like this:

	OPTIONS=gender:male
	#OPTIONS=name:Dutch,role:Archeologist
	#OPTIONS=name:Fezzik,role:Barbarian
	#OPTIONS=name:Bob,role:Tourist
	OPTIONS=name:Fagan,role:Rogue
	#OPTIONS=name:Mitsubishi,role:Samurai,align:lawful

and uncheck whatever option you'd like to play. An advantage of playing 
characters of different names is that you don't have to worry about the 
shopkeeper-perpetually-angry-at-your-character problem.

